Day three of #MilanFashionWeek was a blend of old-school elegance and new-school experimentation. From a surprise #GossipGirl reunion at @MaxMara to @MeryllRogge.Personal’s sophomore show at Marni, here are our highlights.

@MaxMara started things off with a return to reality and true elegance, said creative director Ian Griffiths backstage.

Meryll Rogge presented her second collection for Marni, crystallizing her kooky-yet-precise vision for the house.

Photo: @StyleDuMonde

Emerging talent Francesco Murano’s sci-fi-inspired collection showed his skills in draping jersey into intricate forms.

@EmporioArmani staged a presentation and party at the Teatro Armani, in anticipation of Dario Vitale’s debut show next season.

